// PR-F3 (2026-07-21) — shadow caster (depth-only) with conditional
// VS segment for skinned vs static geometry. ShadowPass acquires
// this material via inline Phoskia source (mirror of
// postprocess.phoskia + simple_lit_shadow.phoskia co-located
// pattern). The `Skeleton` UBO + `boneindices/boneweights` vertex
// semantics are exact mirrors of AYShader/unittest/golden/
// skinned_lit.phoskia — the SAME bone palette goes to whatever
// GpuMaterial is also drawing the model on the FO pass, and the
// caster reads it from this program the same way.
//
// Why double-segment VS:
//   - Static meshes may not have a Skeleton UBO or bone index/weight
//     channels in their vertex layout. A single-segment VS that
//     always calls `skinningMatrix(...)` would crash Phoskia
//     analysis when the host feeds a GpuMesh without those vertex
//     inputs (currently a re-layout landmine in Test_SkinWeightUpload).
//   - Per-mesh code paths in Phoskia are not available (no `var
//     hasBones` runtime dispatch). Conditional `if (jointCount > 0)`
//     in the fragment does not see vertex-shader output, so the
//     branch has to live inside `vertex { ... }`.
//
//   Currently the conditional is a Phoskia property
//   `castSkinned` that the host (`ShadowPass::execute`) writes via
//   shader.setUniform — `castSkinned` == 0 → static path, `==`1 →
//   skinned path. Per-draw `if` on a uniform is the cheapest
//   branch + aligns with our "every material has uniform space"
//   convention.
//
// Fragment body: bgfx depth-only FBO has no color attachment;
// the fragment output is discarded by the hardware. We still must
// emit a `vec4(0.0, ...)` to satisfy Phoskia's "fragment must
// return a value" analyzer. The actual color value doesn't
// propagate.
material ShadowCaster {
    uniformblock Skeleton {
        mat4 bones[128]
    }
    property castSkinned = 0

    vertex {
        in pos    : position
        in boneId : boneindices
        in boneWt : boneweights

        if (castSkinned == 1) {
            let skinned = skinningMatrix(boneId, boneWt, Skeleton.bones, vec4(pos, 1.0))
            return modelViewProjection * skinned
        } else {
            return modelViewProjection * vec4(pos, 1.0)
        }
    }
    fragment {
        return vec4(0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0)
    }
}
